            <ArticleTitle>Orthopaedic patients' reporting of pain management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>43-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Advances in pain management have occurred in recent years through the development of patient-controlled and epidural analgesia, while the conventional regime of intramuscular analgesia has also continued to be used. This article describes a study comparing orthopaedic patients' experiences of postoperative pain using the three methods of analgesia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
